# adblock stack — Pi-hole plus a local recursive Unbound.
#
# ./setup.sh copies this to adblock/.env when that file does not exist yet. A
# stack that ships its own .env.example takes precedence over the repo-root
# one, which is why TLD and TZ appear here as well — but TLD is only ever set
# in the root .env.example: @TLD@ below is expanded from it at copy time, so
# renaming the domain means editing the root .env and re-running ./setup.sh,
# never this file.
#
# adblock/.env is gitignored.

TLD=@TLD@
TZ=Pacific/Auckland

# There is no Pi-hole password: https://pihole.$TLD/admin is behind authentik
# (the authentik stack), and that login is the only one. An older adblock/.env
# may still have a PIHOLE_PASSWORD line — nothing reads it any more.
#
# What keeps the UI from being open on Pi-hole's own LAN address is a web ACL
# that only lets app-bridge (Traefik) in. ./setup.sh appends that subnet here
# as APP_BRIDGE_SUBNET and keeps it current; without it only localhost gets in.

# Pi-hole's address on the router's Docker.Online VLAN (192.168.40.0/24).
# The router is .1 and its DHCP pool is .100-.249, so this is well clear.
# Unbound has no VLAN address — it lives on a private bridge inside this stack,
# which is why there is no UNBOUND_IP to set here.
PIHOLE_IP=192.168.40.5
